      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, looks like the responder key hash doesn\u0027t match the included cert. RFC 6960 has this to say:\n\n\"The purpose of the ResponderID information is to allow clients to\n   find the certificate used to sign a signed OCSP response.  Therefore,\n   the information MUST correspond to the certificate that was used to\n   sign the response.\"\n\nSo IMO this response is not really conforming. OTOH, it is a bit silly to fail the signature check for this, since the signature actually matches. I\u0027ll just remove it again.",
